      "problem": "Evaluate $\\frac{\\sqrt{48}}{\\sqrt{27}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "A quotient of square roots of two positive numbers is equal to the square root of the quotient of the numbers. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{48}}{\\sqrt{27}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{48}{27}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{9}}=\\sqrt{{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$",
